Z||000006||HYPTNOTiSE||12-11-2000||02:39 AM||||The great thing about that engine is the short stroke and the large bore, it probably still gets RPM's very fast.  Also the compression is decent at 10.5:1, and I think the intake system gives the hp a big boost. If you want to make high HP numbers you're going to need short intake runners and a large TB like this has.  I'd probably give a testicle away for that engine. <P>Things i'd change:  Longer rods would be used. They'd be aluminum. I'd use an aluminum flywheel, I would use Gen3 heads and a solid roller cam. <P>Something else to consider.  Wouldn't it be cool to make a 2.8 liter dohc engine. That thing would rev like crazy with such a short stroke! ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||12-11-2000||10:14 AM||||With your suggested form of payment, you might want the longer rod!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||12-12-2000||03:15 AM||||bahahahahahahaha   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>You know, I was thinking about a 2.8 DOHC not too long ago.  If I had a lot of money, I would love to get a 2.8 block and a set of 3.4 TDC heads and figure out what had to be done to mate the two...  just wait 'till I win the lottery  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>On a similar note, is it possible to de-stroke the 3.4 TDC to 3.1?  Beef up the internals and you'd have one hell of a revver, and it'd still have some torque down low.  Another lotto project  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||lou_dias||12-12-2000||12:27 PM||||In the GM performance parts catalog, they sold 12.5:1 pistons for the 2.8<BR>This is going back to the '96 catalog that I have though.<P>Anybody know how to modify a Camaro 3.4 block to accept a roller cam?||||reg||1
